@clawsweeper re-review

All three findings from the `3c8fe6311c7` review are resolved on `b490bd9b537fb2a856f250fae75f251744f04bc4` with focused regressions:

- bare default-session ownership fallback;
- palette-only roster/key/request budgets;
- metadata results retained with a partial-search notice when FTS fails.

The PR body now includes refreshed exact-head production-build, real Gateway/SQLite FTS, screenshot, and browser-video proof.

@clawsweeper re-review

Resolved the latest completeness findings on exact head `32ce8ccca77807c232ed9cad23357753cd4d0aea`:

- successful `indexing` and `truncated` FTS responses now surface the partial-search notice while retaining metadata results;
- a terminal roster of exactly 200 keys is no longer falsely marked truncated;
- added focused regressions for both states and the exact-cap boundary.

Also extended the same palette to lazily search bounded automation, skill, plugin, app, agent, settings, and model/provider catalogs. Full validation and production build are documented in the PR body.

@clawsweeper re-review

Resolved the exact-head wording finding on `6207636026c7230b37a486c0ad3cb2d022feb95c`:

- unavailable FTS now retains the existing unavailable/metadata-only notice;
- successful indexing or truncated responses now show distinct incomplete-results copy;
- the regression includes a transcript-only hit plus each successful partial status.

Validation: 29 focused unit tests, 11 browser E2E tests, full `check:changed`, production Control UI build/budgets, and local autoreview all pass.
